          "passage": "Certain ants gather sugary honeydew from aphids that feed on plants. The same ants also chase away ladybugs and other insects that prey on the aphids. Entomologist Tomas Nilsson hypothesizes that the ants protect the aphids in exchange for honeydew, so that aphid colonies with more attenâ€ tive ant guards should both lose fewer aphids to predators and yield more honeydew to the ants than colonies with fewer guards.",
