          "template": "rw_notes",
          "passage": "While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n\nA geodesic dome is a rounded structure whose surface is divided into a network of triangles. Popularized by designer Buckminster Fuller in the mid-1900s, such domes can span large spaâ€ ces without interior support columns.\n\nA triangle is the only shape that cannot be pushed out of form without bending one of its sides.\n\nWhen a load presses on a geodesic dome, the triangles spread that force evenly across the whole structure.\n\nAs a result, a geodesic dome can be built from relatively little material yet still support heavy loads.",
